<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem difficulty correlates with verification TPR on per-problem level across three domains.</span> Each boxplot shows the distribution of per-problem <math id="A3.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TPR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>TPR</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TPR}</annotation></semantics></math> for 15 verifier models, grouped by difficulty quartiles. <math id="A3.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TPR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>TPR</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TPR}</annotation></semantics></math> exhibits a strong positive correlation with problem easiness: easier problems consistently yield higher and less variable <math id="A3.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TPR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>TPR</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TPR}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
